WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.868
-You're one of my faves.
-Likewise.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:06.767
-I was looking at your résumé.
I'm looking through your stuff.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:09.000
And you've been acting
for 20 years?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.901
-Yeah. 20 years this year.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.734
-You're not even 20 years old.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.534
-I'm only 25, yeah.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.334
I'm only 25.
-But that's wild.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.000
-I know.
It's a little crazy to me.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.701
It was funny.
When I was 10 years old --

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.567
I was 5 years old, and I
realized -- I was like --

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:23.767
I looked at my mom
and I was like,

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:26.000
"When I'm 10, am I gonna get
my tenure?"

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.000
-Oh, is that right?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.968
-I thought that tenure was
ten-year.

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.367
-Ten year, yeah.
"Am I gonna get my tenure?"

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:31.934
-And it was not true.
-No, it's not.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:34.634
I have a picture of you
from your --

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.801
You were in "The Amityville
Horror," by the way.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:39.267
-Yes.
This was my first feature film.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.501
[ Audience aws ]

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.300
-At age 5, were you even allowed
to see this movie?

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.968
-I was not allowed to see
this movie at all.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:47.501
-Oh, here's you and Ryan
Reynolds, who was in the movie.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.934
-Look at that little,
huge smile.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.868
[ Laughter ]
-He's so happy.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.567
-She's very excited.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:56.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.901 --> 00:01:00.501
-Yeah. It was really funny
because most of my career

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:04.734
at that age, I was doing kind of
more R-rated or PG-13 movies.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:08.000
So my mom would have to wait
until the movies came out on DVD

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.033
and then do, like,
a little highlights reel.

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:13.601
And so just kind of fast-forward
and show me -- just me --

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.067
which is like 10 minutes.
-Yeah, and then you'd never got

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.467
to see any movie
you were ever in.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.100
-Yeah. Exactly.
-You know, every time you're

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.801
here, you always teach me about
a new hobby

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.167
that you're getting into.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.868
And this time, I go,
"Are you into anything new?"

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.534
And you go, "Yeah."
-Yeah.

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.701
-Dirt bikes.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.801
-No, this is scaring me.
Like, look at this.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.200
This is how cool you look.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you, guys.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.968
Thank you very much.
-What got you into it?

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:39.567
How long have you been doing it?
-So I grew up kind of

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.567
doing ATVs, but I was never
allowed to dirt bike.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.033
My mom was super against it.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.100
So obviously I grew up and I was
like, "I'm gonna do it."

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.501
I'm going to immediately
go for it.

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.601
-That's what every kid does.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:51.100
But it's really like -- The
thing is is when I'm on contract

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.567
and filming, I'm not allowed to
do anything dangerous.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.267
You can't roller blade
or anything.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:57.000
-Yeah.
-So when I'm off contract,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.834
I'm like, "Let's go for it."

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:00.834
And this is the latest one.

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:02.167
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:06.234
I mean, but it doesn't scare you
at all to go that fast?

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.868
For me, I'm just like --
I don't want anything fast.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:12.000
-I really like going fast.
And I actually really want to

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.834
get into, like -- I want to try
to do, like, motocross jumps,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.100
which are kind of scary.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.067
-So I had my version of
my first motocross jump

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:20.667
very recently last week.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:24.367
And I flew over this thing,
and I felt that it was

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.767
the biggest jump
anyone had ever done.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.868
-You actually brought video
to show our audience tonight.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.868
Here's Chloe Grace Moretz
attempting

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.367
her first dirt bike jump.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:34.868
Check this out.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.367
[ Engine revving ]

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:38.767
[ Laughs ]

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:43.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.434
-Did we get to -- Did we get to
the -- Did we get to the part?

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.300
-He's laughing. It was so loud.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.968
-Did we get to the part
where you jumped?

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:53.667
-I -- You seriously -- I think I
flew way more than the bike.

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.667
I was like, "Whoa!"

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:56.734
-Thank you for bringing
that video.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.133
That's crazy.
That's pretty cool.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.667
I want to talk about about
"The Peripheral," by the way.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.467
-Yes.
-I love the premise.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:04.300
Can we explain what this series
is about?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.667
-Yeah, it's about a young woman
named Flynne Fisher,

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:09.300
and she lives in a small town
in the Appalachian Mountains.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.100
And basically she video-games
for a living.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.567
She plays simulation games.
And she plays it for

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:17.601
wealthy folks who pretty much
want them to level up

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:20.400
their avatars -- wants her
to level up the avatars.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.467
And so one day, she thinks she's
beta-testing a new headset.

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:28.567
And she puts it on, and
immediately she realizes that

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.801
she's not operating
a simulation game

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:35.200
but she's operating a robot body
in the year 2099 in London.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.701
-That's what I'm talking about.
-Yeah.

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.567
So it's really great.

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.267
-You realize you're not playing
a video game.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.634
"Wait a second.
This is actually real."

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.000
-Yeah. And she basically becomes

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.968
a little bit of
a government pawn.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:48.667
And so it's trying to figure out
how she can figure out the world

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.567
that she's been placed in,
which has real-world problems

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:55.234
in the sense that people in her
time in 2032 are now trying to

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.534
come and kill her
and her family.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.667
-I think it's fantastic.
I love the idea. It's so good.

00:03:58.667 --> 00:03:59.834
And you were telling me

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.701
there's a lot of action
sequences in this.

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:05.767
And you were saying, yeah, you
tried to learn judo, was it?

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.033
-Yeah, judo.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:08.534
-Since, what, from "Kick-Ass"?

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:10.100
-Yeah, so I started doing
martial arts

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.033
when I was 11 in "Kick-Ass."
And I got to train for --

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:13.634
[ Single cheer ]
Yeah, thank you.

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:14.968
[ Laughter ]
I got to train -- It's cool.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.267
Martial arts is tight.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:19.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.033
And for this one, our wonderful
stunt coordinator,

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:24.534
Tony, he's a master judo
champion.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.834
And he really wanted me to get
into it.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:31.434
And I was super down because it
means I can throw 160-,

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:35.701
180-pound men just, like, over
my shoulder and just fly them,

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:37.067
which sounds so fun.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.400
-Yeah. You can do that.
-Yes.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.267
-And thank goodness we're not
doing it to me.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.934
But you brought video as well.
-I did offer.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.868
I was like,
"I will do it to you."

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.434
We don't have to do it.

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:49.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.601
-Do it!

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:51.734
-I mean, you want to do it?

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:52.734
-No.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:54.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:58.033
-Can you?
Am I going to get hurt?

00:04:58.033 --> 00:04:59.501
-I don't think so.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.267
You might get hurt.
-I might get hurt?

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.400
-Do it!

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.701
-I mean, do you want to?

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:06.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.667
Where do I land?
What do I have to do?

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:10.934
-You can land on the couch.
-I can land on the couch?

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:12.133
-Yeah, watch this.
Okay, come here.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.968
-Uh-huh. Seriously, we did not
rehearse this.

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:15.934
-No, we did not rehearse this.
Okay, put your arm up.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.100
-You know I love you. I'm a fan.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:20.133
-Put your arm up.
-Uh-huh.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.534
-And then I'm going to go
underneath you.

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.467
And you're going to come around.
And then --

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:28.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:29.868
-I'm too old!

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:33.000
I'm too old to be thrown!

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.067
Here's a clip from
"The Peripheral."

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.801
Here's Chloe Grace Moretz.

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.100
Check it out.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.834
-Don't care to lecture me
about pain.

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:43.367
-Well, I don't want to
lecture you.

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:45.167
I just want to snap
your [bleep] neck.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:48.834
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.968
Do you feel it?

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:53.534
Darkness closing in.

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:58.968
Let it be preparation for when I
kill you and it's real.

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:16.033
-I got a foothold
in your world now.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:19.200
So next time I'll be coming
for you instead.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.067
-Yeah, that's how you do it
right there!

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:23.167
Chloe Grace Moretz, everybody.

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:25.000
New episodes of "The Peripheral"

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.400
are available Fridays
on Prime Video.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.634
We'll be right back with

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:30.634
a performance from Bruce
Springsteen. Stick around.

